course: dictionary
lesson: 3946
title: One word, three meanings: fun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fun is a small word with several meanings. The words around it tell you which one you need. «We had fun at the party» uses fun as a noun. It names the enjoyment and good time you have.
explain: «A fun game» uses fun as an adjective. It describes the game, so the game is enjoyable. Check by swapping in another word: «an enjoyable game» still makes sense.
explain: The third meaning is different. To make fun of someone means to laugh at them in an unkind way. Look at the sentence: if someone is being laughed at unkindly, it is not fun for them, even if others are laughing.
fact: Fun can be a noun: «We had fun at the party» means enjoyment and a good time.
fact: Fun can be an adjective: «a fun game» means a game that is enjoyable.
fact: «Make fun of» someone means to laugh at them in an unkind way, and it hurts.
fact: A prank is only fun when everyone is laughing, including the person it is played on.
fact: Fun, more fun and most fun are the standard forms; some people informally say funner and funnest.
exercise: What does fun mean in «We had fun at the party»? | A kind of food served at parties | A loud noise | Money paid for a party | *Enjoyment and a good time
exercise: What does «make fun of» mean? | Give someone a present to cheer them up | *Laugh at someone in an unkind way | Ask someone to join a game | Hug a friend who is sad
exercise: In «a fun game», what kind of word is fun? | A noun | *An adjective, meaning enjoyable | A verb, meaning to play | A name for the game
test: According to «A prank can be fun if everyone laughs together, including the person tricked», what makes a prank fun? | It is a lie that upsets people | It is done in secret, with no one told | *Everyone laughs together, including the person tricked | It makes one person cry
test: Which sentence uses fun as an adjective? | She had a lot of fun at the fair. | We went out just for fun. | *They invented a fun game for the class.
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of fun? | Enjoyment and a good time | *Lost, far from home | Enjoyable, like a fun game | To laugh at someone in an unkind way
